examples.question_text:
The numbers show the capacities of the directed edges.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{flow/.style={decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.6 with {\arrow{>}}},postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (S) at (0,1.5);
\coordinate (A) at (2,3);
\coordinate (B) at (3,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.5,3);
\coordinate (T) at (6.5,1.5);
\draw[flow] (S)--(A) node[midway,above left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$12$};
\draw[flow] (S)--(B) node[midway,below left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$7$};
\draw[flow] (A)--(C) node[midway,above,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$6$};
\draw[flow] (A)--(B) node[midway,left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$3$};
\draw[flow] (C)--(T) node[midway,above right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$9$};
\draw[flow] (B)--(T) node[midway,below right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$10$};
\fill[black] (S) circle (2pt) node[left] {$S$};
\fill[black] (A) circle (2pt) node[above] {$A$};
\fill[black] (B) circle (2pt) node[below] {$B$};
\fill[black] (C) circle (2pt) node[above] {$C$};
\fill[black] (T) circle (2pt) node[right] {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
a. Push the greatest possible flow along $S\to A\to C\to T$. Find the remaining capacity of $SA$.
b. Continue with $S\to A\to B\to T$, then $S\to B\to T$. Determine the maximum flow.
c. List the saturated edges and the edges that are not saturated after this allocation.

examples.solution_text:
a. The first path carries $\min(12,6,9)=6$.
The remaining capacity of $SA$ is
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}12-6\\&=6\end{aligned}$
Subtract $6$ from every edge on this path: $SA$, $AC$ and $CT$ have remaining capacities $6$, $0$ and $3$.

b. The three source-to-sink paths are $S\to A\to C\to T$, $S\to A\to B\to T$ and $S\to B\to T$.
The second path carries $\min(6,3,10)=3$. This leaves $SA=3$, $AB=0$ and $BT=7$.
The third path carries $\min(7,7)=7$. This leaves $SB=0$ and $BT=0$.
The total flow is
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}6+3+7\\&=16\end{aligned}$
Every source-to-sink path uses either $AC$ or $BT$. Their original capacities total $6+10=16$, so the maximum flow is $16$.

c. The diagram shows the final remaining capacities.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{flow/.style={decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.6 with {\arrow{>}}},postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (S) at (0,1.5);
\coordinate (A) at (2,3);
\coordinate (B) at (3,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.5,3);
\coordinate (T) at (6.5,1.5);
\draw[flow] (S)--(A) node[midway,above left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$3$};
\draw[flow] (S)--(B) node[midway,below left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$0$};
\draw[flow] (A)--(C) node[midway,above,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$0$};
\draw[flow] (A)--(B) node[midway,left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$0$};
\draw[flow] (C)--(T) node[midway,above right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$3$};
\draw[flow] (B)--(T) node[midway,below right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$0$};
\fill[black] (S) circle (2pt) node[left] {$S$};
\fill[black] (A) circle (2pt) node[above] {$A$};
\fill[black] (B) circle (2pt) node[below] {$B$};
\fill[black] (C) circle (2pt) node[above] {$C$};
\fill[black] (T) circle (2pt) node[right] {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The saturated edges are $SB$, $AC$, $AB$ and $BT$: each has zero remaining capacity.
The edges that are not saturated are $SA$ and $CT$: each has $3$ remaining.

