Water flows from $S$ to $T$. Each edge capacity is in litres per minute.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{flow/.style={decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.6 with {\arrow{>}}},postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (S) at (0,1.5);
\coordinate (A) at (2,3);
\coordinate (B) at (2.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.5,3);
\coordinate (D) at (4.5,0);
\coordinate (T) at (6.5,1.5);
\draw[flow] (S)--(A) node[midway,above left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$6$};
\draw[flow] (S)--(B) node[midway,below left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$10$};
\draw[flow] (A)--(C) node[midway,above,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$8$};
\draw[flow] (A)--(B) node[midway,left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\draw[flow] (B)--(D) node[midway,below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$8$};
\draw[flow] (C)--(T) node[midway,above right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$9$};
\draw[flow] (D)--(T) node[midway,below right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$11$};
\fill[black] (S) circle (2pt) node[left] {$S$};
\fill[black] (A) circle (2pt) node[above] {$A$};
\fill[black] (B) circle (2pt) node[below] {$B$};
\fill[black] (C) circle (2pt) node[above] {$C$};
\fill[black] (D) circle (2pt) node[below] {$D$};
\fill[black] (T) circle (2pt) node[right] {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Determine the maximum flow by considering every source-to-sink path, starting with the top path. Explain why one path carries no additional flow.
